<div class="docs-getstarted-page">

  <h1 class="docs-getstarted-title">Theming</h1>
  <p class="docs-getstarted-desc">Customize SoftUI to match your brand by overriding CSS custom properties. No build tools needed.</p>

  <!-- How It Works -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="how-it-works">
    <h2>How It Works</h2>
    <p>SoftUI is built entirely on CSS custom properties (<code>--sui-*</code>). Override them on <code>:root</code> to change the look of every component at once.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>:root {
  --sui-primary: #7C5CFC;         /* Your brand color */
  --sui-radius: 12px;             /* Sharper or rounder corners */
  --sui-font: 'Inter', sans-serif; /* Your font */
}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;">That's it. Every button, card, input, and component will update automatically.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Colors -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="colors">
    <h2>Colors</h2>
    <p>The color system has 5 semantic colors, each with a hover variant. Fills, borders, shadows and icons use these base tokens.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>:root {
  /* Primary — buttons, links, active states */
  --sui-primary: #5B54E0;
  --sui-primary-hover: #4A44C4;

  /* Success — confirmations, positive actions */
  --sui-success: #198758;
  --sui-success-hover: #126D47;

  /* Danger — errors, destructive actions */
  --sui-danger: #D03A5C;
  --sui-danger-hover: #B42E4C;

  /* Warning — caution, pending states */
  --sui-warning: #F5A623;
  --sui-warning-hover: #DB921A;

  /* Info — informational, neutral highlights */
  --sui-info: #187AC8;
  --sui-info-hover: #1364A3;
}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;"><strong>Text shades.</strong> Colored <em>text</em> (links, outline and ghost buttons, outline badges and chips, alerts, <code>.sui-text-*</code> utilities, active nav items) uses a separate <code>-text</code> token that reaches WCAG AA (4.5:1) on every plain <code>--sui-bg*</code> surface of the theme. On tinted hover and active surfaces (selected items, ghost-button hover, range highlights) components switch to the <code>-text-hover</code> shade, which keeps 4.5:1. Each theme block sets its own values — dark mode uses lighter shades.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>:root {
  --sui-primary-text: #4D45DD;   --sui-primary-text-hover: #3A31DA;
  --sui-success-text: #136A45;   --sui-success-text-hover: #115C3C;
  --sui-danger-text: #AE2947;    --sui-danger-text-hover: #97243E;
  --sui-warning-text: #825306;   --sui-warning-text-hover: #714805;
  --sui-info-text: #13609D;      --sui-info-text-hover: #115388;

  /* Text on a warning fill (buttons, badges, chips, filled alerts) */
  --sui-warning-contrast: #2D3748;
}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);">If you override <code>--sui-primary</code> (or another semantic color), also set the matching <code>-text</code> and <code>-text-hover</code> tokens for each theme — on <code>:root, [data-theme="light"]</code> and on <code>[data-theme="dark"]</code> (the light block redeclares them, so a <code>:root</code>-only override is reset inside light scopes and leaks into dark mode). Pick shades with at least 4.5:1 contrast on every <code>--sui-bg*</code> of that theme: the darkest one, <code>--sui-bg-dark</code>, in light mode; the lightest one, <code>--sui-bg-light</code>, in dark mode.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;"><strong>Tints and focus rings.</strong> Hover tints, glows and focus rings are mixed from the color tokens with <code>color-mix()</code>, so they follow your brand color automatically (Chrome/Edge 111+, Safari 16.2+, Firefox 113+). The focus ring has two optional overrides:</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>:root {
  /* Just the color (default: --sui-primary at 40%) */
  --sui-focus-ring-color: color-mix(in srgb, #0066FF 50%, transparent);

  /* Or the whole ring (default: 0 0 0 3px var(--sui-focus-ring-color)) */
  --sui-focus-ring: 0 0 0 2px #fff, 0 0 0 4px #0066FF;
}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;"><strong>Links.</strong> Bare <code>&lt;a&gt;</code>, <code>.sui-link</code>, <code>.sui-link-subtle</code> and <code>.sui-link-arrow</code> read three optional tokens. Unset, they fall back to <code>--sui-primary-text</code> / <code>--sui-primary-text-hover</code>, so they follow the theme (including scoped <code>data-theme</code> areas). If you set them, set them per theme like the <code>-text</code> tokens, and keep 4.5:1 contrast on every <code>--sui-bg*</code>.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>:root, [data-theme="light"] {
  --sui-link: #0057B8;         /* default: var(--sui-primary-text) */
  --sui-link-hover: #00428C;   /* default: var(--sui-primary-text-hover) */
  /* Underline colour of .sui-link / -subtle / -muted at rest
     (default: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 40%, transparent)) */
  --sui-link-underline: currentColor;
}
[data-theme="dark"] {
  --sui-link: #7DB8FF;
  --sui-link-hover: #A6CEFF;
}</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Backgrounds -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="backgrounds">
    <h2>Backgrounds & Surfaces</h2>
    <p>Three background shades create the neumorphic depth. <code>bg</code> is the base, <code>bg-light</code> is slightly lighter, <code>bg-dark</code> is slightly darker.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>:root {
  --sui-bg: #E4E9F0;       /* Base surface */
  --sui-bg-light: #EDF1F7;  /* Lighter (raised highlights) */
  --sui-bg-dark: #D1D9E6;   /* Darker (borders, tracks) */
}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;">These three values work together to create the soft shadow illusion. When changing them, keep them close in tone — the effect breaks if they're too far apart.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Shadows -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="shadows">
    <h2>Shadows</h2>
    <p>Neumorphic shadows use two colors: a dark shadow (bottom-right) and a light shadow (top-left). These are combined into preset shadow values.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>:root {
  /* Shadow colors */
  --sui-shadow-light: #FFFFFF;
  --sui-shadow-dark: #B8C0CC;

  /* Raised (outward) shadows */
  --sui-shadow-raised-sm: 3px 3px 8px var(--sui-shadow-dark),
                          -3px -3px 8px var(--sui-shadow-light);
  --sui-shadow-raised:    6px 6px 14px var(--sui-shadow-dark),
                          -6px -6px 14px var(--sui-shadow-light);
  --sui-shadow-raised-lg: 10px 10px 20px var(--sui-shadow-dark),
                          -10px -10px 20px var(--sui-shadow-light);

  /* Inset (pressed) shadows */
  --sui-shadow-inset:    inset 3px 3px 8px var(--sui-shadow-dark),
                         inset -3px -3px 8px var(--sui-shadow-light);
  --sui-shadow-inset-sm: inset 2px 2px 5px var(--sui-shadow-dark),
                         inset -2px -2px 5px var(--sui-shadow-light);
}

/* Tip: just changing --sui-shadow-light and --sui-shadow-dark
   updates ALL shadows automatically */</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Text -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="text">
    <h2>Text Colors</h2>
    <p>Three text color tiers for hierarchy.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>:root {
  --sui-text: #2D3748;       /* Primary text — headings, body */
  --sui-text-muted: #4D5A6D;  /* Secondary — descriptions, labels */
  --sui-text-light: #526072;  /* Tertiary — hints, placeholders */
}</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Border Radius -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="radius">
    <h2>Border Radius</h2>
    <p>Five radius tokens control the roundness across all components.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>:root {
  --sui-radius-xs: 6px;        /* Small elements (chips, badges) */
  --sui-radius-sm: 10px;       /* Inputs, buttons */
  --sui-radius: 16px;          /* Cards, modals */
  --sui-radius-lg: 24px;       /* Large containers */
  --sui-radius-full: 9999px;   /* Pills, circles */
}

/* Sharp look */
:root {
  --sui-radius-xs: 2px;
  --sui-radius-sm: 4px;
  --sui-radius: 6px;
  --sui-radius-lg: 8px;
}

/* Extra round */
:root {
  --sui-radius-xs: 10px;
  --sui-radius-sm: 14px;
  --sui-radius: 20px;
  --sui-radius-lg: 32px;
}</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Typography -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="typography">
    <h2>Typography</h2>
    <p>Change the font family used across all components.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>:root {
  --sui-font: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', 'Plus Jakarta Sans Variable', -apple-system,
              BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, sans-serif;
}

/* Use Inter */
:root {
  --sui-font: 'Inter', sans-serif;
}

/* Use system fonts only (no Google Fonts) */
:root {
  --sui-font: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI',
              Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, sans-serif;
}

/* Monospace font (code, kbd, shortcuts, OTP, Copy Button, Color Picker) */
:root {
  --sui-font-mono: 'JetBrains Mono', 'JetBrains Mono Variable', 'Fira Code',
                   'Cascadia Code', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo,
                   Consolas, monospace;
}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;"><strong>Loading the fonts.</strong> SoftUI doesn't bundle any fonts. Plus Jakarta Sans and JetBrains Mono are only used if your page loads them; otherwise each stack falls back to the system fonts listed after them. Pick one of these:</p>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;">1. Google Fonts — add to your <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, before the SoftUI stylesheet:</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"&gt;
&lt;link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin&gt;
&lt;link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&amp;family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&amp;display=swap" rel="stylesheet"&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;">2. Self-hosted with Fontsource — the <code>'… Variable'</code> family names are already in the default stacks, so no override is needed:</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>npm i @fontsource-variable/plus-jakarta-sans @fontsource-variable/jetbrains-mono

/* In your entry file */
import '@fontsource-variable/plus-jakarta-sans';
import '@fontsource-variable/jetbrains-mono';</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;">3. Nothing — skip both and SoftUI renders in the system UI and monospace fonts.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Component Variables -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="component-vars">
    <h2>Component Variables</h2>
    <p>Some components expose their own CSS variables for fine-tuning.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>/* Modal — backdrop blur amount */
.sui-modal-backdrop {
  --sui-modal-blur: 6px;  /* or use classes: sui-modal-blur-none/sm/md/lg/xl */
}

/* Stack — hover spread distance and multiplier */
.sui-stack-hover {
  --sui-stack-gap: 180px;    /* base spread distance (match your card width) */
  --sui-stack-spread: 0.6;   /* multiplier (0.15 to 1) */
}

/* Sections — vertical rhythm for .sui-section / .sui-section-header */
:root {
  --sui-section-space: 96px;     /* .sui-section padding (64px below 768px) */
  --sui-section-space-sm: 64px;  /* .sui-section-sm, and .sui-section on mobile */
  --sui-section-space-xs: 40px;  /* .sui-section-sm on mobile */
  --sui-section-header-gap: 40px; /* space below .sui-section-header */
}

/* Heading accent bar — optional, defaults to var(--sui-primary).
   Not declared on :root, so it follows --sui-primary wherever that is set;
   set it on any ancestor, e.g. a lighter bar for more contrast on dark: */
[data-theme="dark"] {
  --sui-heading-accent: #8C86F0;
}</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Transitions -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="transitions">
    <h2>Transitions</h2>
    <p>Three speed tokens for animation timing.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>:root {
  --sui-transition-fast: 0.15s;  /* Hover states, toggles */
  --sui-transition-base: 0.25s;  /* Most animations */
  --sui-transition-slow: 0.35s;  /* Page transitions, modals */
  --sui-transition: all var(--sui-transition-base) ease;
}

/* Snappier feel */
:root {
  --sui-transition-fast: 0.1s;
  --sui-transition-base: 0.15s;
  --sui-transition-slow: 0.25s;
}

/* Disable all transitions */
:root {
  --sui-transition-fast: 0s;
  --sui-transition-base: 0s;
  --sui-transition-slow: 0s;
}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);"><strong>Reduced motion.</strong> When the user sets <code>prefers-reduced-motion: reduce</code>, CSS transitions and animations become near-instant, and <code>softui.js</code> turns off its own motion: carousel autoplay stops, text rotate stays on its first word, typewriters show their text immediately, radial progress shows its final value, scroll reveal shows content straight away, and scrollspy/tour links jump instead of scrolling smoothly. No setup needed.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Dark Mode -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="dark-mode">
    <h2>Dark Mode</h2>
    <p>Dark mode overrides backgrounds, shadows, and text colors. Add <code>data-theme="dark"</code> to your <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> element.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;html data-theme="dark"&gt;

/* Dark mode variables (already built-in) */
[data-theme="dark"] {
  --sui-bg: #2A2D35;
  --sui-bg-light: #31343C;
  --sui-bg-dark: #23262D;

  --sui-shadow-light: #33363F;
  --sui-shadow-dark: #1E2027;

  --sui-text: #E2E8F0;
  --sui-text-muted: #9BA5B8;
  --sui-text-light: #939CAD;

  /* Colored text goes lighter in dark mode */
  --sui-primary-text: #9894EC;   --sui-primary-text-hover: #ADAAF0;
  --sui-success-text: #21B374;   --sui-success-text-hover: #25CA83;
  --sui-danger-text: #E18197;    --sui-danger-text-hover: #E89DAE;
  --sui-warning-text: #F5A623;   --sui-warning-text-hover: #F8BB55;
  --sui-info-text: #4BA4E9;      --sui-info-text-hover: #73B8EE;
}

/* Custom dark theme */
[data-theme="dark"] {
  --sui-bg: #1A1A2E;
  --sui-bg-light: #222240;
  --sui-bg-dark: #141427;
  --sui-primary: #9B59B6;
  --sui-primary-text: #C39BD3;
}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;"><strong>Scoped themes.</strong> <code>data-theme</code> works on any element, not just <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>. Use <code>data-theme="dark"</code> or <code>data-theme="light"</code> on a section to give it its own theme. Pair it with <code>.sui-surface</code> so the section paints the matching background — see <a href="/getting-started/#existing-sites" style="color:var(--sui-primary-text);font-weight:600;">Using in an Existing Site</a>.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;section class="sui-surface" data-theme="dark"&gt;
  &lt;!-- Dark SoftUI components on a light page --&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);">Scoped sections set their own background, shadow, text and component tokens (tints, select arrow, scrollbars), so a light section inside a dark page fully resets. If you customize these, override them on <code>[data-theme]</code> as well as <code>:root</code>.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:14px;color:var(--sui-text-muted);"><strong>Dark theme on a darker page:</strong> on a background darker than <code>--sui-bg</code> (for example pure black), the light half of dark-mode shadows shows as a faint halo. Wrap the area in <code>.sui-surface</code> with <code>data-theme="dark"</code> so it gets the matching background, or use <code>.sui-flat-all</code>.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Dark Mode Toggle -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="dark-mode-toggle">
    <h2>Dark Mode Toggle</h2>
    <p><code>softui.js</code> includes a theme switcher. Add <code>data-sui-theme-toggle</code> to any button and it toggles dark mode, saves the choice, follows the operating system until the user picks one, and stays in sync across tabs. Try these — they control this site:</p>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:24px;align-items:center;margin:16px 0;">
      <button class="sui-theme-toggle" data-sui-theme-toggle aria-label="Dark mode">
        <svg class="sui-theme-toggle-sun" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="5"/><line x1="12" y1="1" x2="12" y2="3"/><line x1="12" y1="21" x2="12" y2="23"/><line x1="4.22" y1="4.22" x2="5.64" y2="5.64"/><line x1="18.36" y1="18.36" x2="19.78" y2="19.78"/><line x1="1" y1="12" x2="3" y2="12"/><line x1="21" y1="12" x2="23" y2="12"/><line x1="4.22" y1="19.78" x2="5.64" y2="18.36"/><line x1="18.36" y1="5.64" x2="19.78" y2="4.22"/></svg>
        <svg class="sui-theme-toggle-moon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 12.79A9 9 0 1111.21 3 7 7 0 0021 12.79z"/></svg>
      </button>
      <button class="sui-swap sui-swap-rotate" data-sui-theme-toggle aria-label="Dark mode">
        <span class="sui-swap-on"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 12.79A9 9 0 1111.21 3 7 7 0 0021 12.79z"/></svg></span>
        <span class="sui-swap-off"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="5"/><line x1="12" y1="1" x2="12" y2="3"/><line x1="12" y1="21" x2="12" y2="23"/><line x1="4.22" y1="4.22" x2="5.64" y2="5.64"/><line x1="18.36" y1="18.36" x2="19.78" y2="19.78"/><line x1="1" y1="12" x2="3" y2="12"/><line x1="21" y1="12" x2="23" y2="12"/><line x1="4.22" y1="19.78" x2="5.64" y2="18.36"/><line x1="18.36" y1="5.64" x2="19.78" y2="4.22"/></svg></span>
      </button>
      <div class="sui-toggle-group" role="group" aria-label="Theme">
        <button class="sui-toggle-group-item" data-sui-theme-toggle="light">Light</button>
        <button class="sui-toggle-group-item" data-sui-theme-toggle="dark">Dark</button>
        <button class="sui-toggle-group-item" data-sui-theme-toggle="system">System</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;!-- Sun/moon button (sun in light, moon in dark) --&gt;
&lt;button class="sui-theme-toggle" data-sui-theme-toggle aria-label="Dark mode"&gt;
  &lt;svg class="sui-theme-toggle-sun" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"&gt;...&lt;/svg&gt;
  &lt;svg class="sui-theme-toggle-moon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"&gt;...&lt;/svg&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;!-- Any swap works too (the moon shows while dark) --&gt;
&lt;button class="sui-swap sui-swap-rotate" data-sui-theme-toggle aria-label="Dark mode"&gt;
  &lt;span class="sui-swap-on"&gt;&lt;!-- moon svg --&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="sui-swap-off"&gt;&lt;!-- sun svg --&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;!-- Set a value instead of toggling --&gt;
&lt;div class="sui-toggle-group" role="group" aria-label="Theme"&gt;
  &lt;button class="sui-toggle-group-item" data-sui-theme-toggle="light"&gt;Light&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;button class="sui-toggle-group-item" data-sui-theme-toggle="dark"&gt;Dark&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;button class="sui-toggle-group-item" data-sui-theme-toggle="system"&gt;System&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;">Add this blocking script to your <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, before the stylesheets, so the saved theme applies before the first paint (no flash of the wrong theme):</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;script&gt;
    try {
      var t = localStorage.getItem('sui-theme');
      if (t !== 'light' &amp;&amp; t !== 'dark')
        t = matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme:dark)').matches ? 'dark' : 'light';
      document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', t);
    } catch (e) {}
  &lt;/script&gt;
  &lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="softui.min.css"&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;"><strong>How it works</strong></p>
    <ul style="margin:8px 0 16px 20px;line-height:1.8;">
      <li><strong>Priority:</strong> the saved choice (<code>localStorage['sui-theme']</code>) wins, then the system preference. <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> always gets an explicit <code>data-theme="light"</code> or <code>"dark"</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Opt-in:</strong> the switcher only runs when the page has a <code>[data-sui-theme-toggle]</code> element, <code>&lt;html data-sui-theme-auto&gt;</code> (follow the system with no button), or when you call the API. Pages that set <code>data-theme</code> by hand are left alone.</li>
      <li><strong>Values:</strong> <code>data-sui-theme-toggle</code> with no value toggles. <code>="light"</code> and <code>="dark"</code> save that theme; <code>="system"</code> clears the saved choice and follows the OS again.</li>
      <li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> toggles get <code>aria-pressed="true"</code> while dark is on, and <code>aria-label="Dark mode"</code> if they have no name. Set-buttons are pressed when they match the saved choice. To swap the label instead, add <code>data-sui-label-dark</code> and <code>data-sui-label-light</code> (the label used while that theme is active) — <code>aria-pressed</code> is then left off.</li>
      <li><strong>Swaps:</strong> a <code>.sui-swap</code> with <code>data-sui-theme-toggle</code> is driven by the switcher (<code>.active</code> = dark) and does not fire <code>sui-swap-change</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Scope:</strong> the switcher controls <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> only. Scoped <code>data-theme</code> sections keep their own theme.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>SoftUI.theme.get();          // 'light' | 'dark' — the current theme
SoftUI.theme.set('dark');    // save and apply
SoftUI.theme.toggle();       // flip and save
SoftUI.theme.clear();        // forget the choice, follow the system
SoftUI.theme.system();       // 'light' | 'dark' — the OS preference

// Fires on every change
document.addEventListener('sui-theme-change', function (e) {
  e.detail.theme;   // 'light' | 'dark'
  e.detail.source;  // 'user' | 'system' | 'storage' (another tab) | 'init'
});</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:16px;"><strong>Without softui.js.</strong> If you only use the CSS, a few lines do the basics:</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>&lt;button onclick="toggleTheme(this)" aria-pressed="false"&gt;Dark mode&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
  function toggleTheme(btn) {
    var html = document.documentElement;
    var next = html.getAttribute('data-theme') === 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark';
    html.setAttribute('data-theme', next);
    btn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(next === 'dark'));
    try { localStorage.setItem('sui-theme', next); } catch (e) {}
  }
&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Full Example -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="example">
    <h2>Full Example</h2>
    <p>A complete brand override — just drop this in your CSS after importing SoftUI.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>/* My Brand Theme */
:root, [data-theme="light"] {
  /* Colors */
  --sui-primary: #0066FF;
  --sui-primary-hover: #0052CC;
  --sui-primary-text: #0052CC;       /* AA on --sui-bg-dark */
  --sui-primary-text-hover: #0043A8;

  /* Surfaces */
  --sui-bg: #F0F2F5;
  --sui-bg-light: #F8F9FA;
  --sui-bg-dark: #E4E6EB;
  --sui-shadow-light: #FFFFFF;
  --sui-shadow-dark: #C8CCD4;

  /* Typography */
  --sui-font: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  --sui-text: #1A1A1A;

  /* Shape */
  --sui-radius: 8px;
  --sui-radius-sm: 4px;
  --sui-radius-lg: 12px;

  /* Speed */
  --sui-transition-base: 0.2s;
}

/* Dark mode: the rule above also matches &lt;html data-theme="dark"&gt;
   (it is :root), so restate the dark surfaces and text here. */
[data-theme="dark"] {
  --sui-bg: #2A2D35;
  --sui-bg-light: #31343C;
  --sui-bg-dark: #23262D;
  --sui-shadow-light: #33363F;
  --sui-shadow-dark: #1E2027;
  --sui-text: #E2E8F0;
  --sui-primary-text: #6EA8FF;       /* AA on --sui-bg-light */
  --sui-primary-text-hover: #8FBBFF;
}</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Design Tokens -->
  <section class="docs-getstarted-section" id="tokens">
    <h2>Design Tokens (JSON)</h2>
    <p>SoftUI ships a <code>tokens.json</code> file with all design values. Use it to sync with Tailwind, Figma plugins, Style Dictionary, or your own design system.</p>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code">
<pre><code>/* Import tokens in JavaScript */
import tokens from 'softui-css/dist/tokens.json';

console.log(tokens.colors.primary);     // "#5B54E0"
console.log(tokens.radius.default);     // "16px"
console.log(tokens.typography.font);    // "'Plus Jakarta Sans', ..."</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-getstarted-code" style="margin-top:16px;">
<pre><code>/* Use with Tailwind CSS */
const tokens = require('softui-css/dist/tokens.json');

module.exports = {
  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: {
        primary: tokens.colors.primary,
        success: tokens.colors.success,
        danger: tokens.colors.danger,
      },
      borderRadius: {
        soft: tokens.radius.default,
        'soft-sm': tokens.radius.sm,
        'soft-lg': tokens.radius.lg,
      }
    }
  }
};</code></pre>
    </div>
